# La pagina de servicios paso a llamarse extras. 301 para no perder lo indexado.
/services      /extras      301
/es/services   /es/extras   301

# Astro genera cada pagina como carpeta/index.html, y Netlify sirve ese archivo
# con 200 en las dos rutas: /packages/ y /packages/index.html. La segunda lleva
# canonical a la primera, y eso es exactamente lo que Search Console reporta
# como "pagina alternativa con etiqueta canonica adecuada". El ! fuerza el
# redirect aunque el archivo exista. Netlify solo admite comodines al final, asi
# que cada nivel de profundidad necesita su regla (la mas honda del sitio es
# /es/blog/posts/slug/).
/index.html                 /                301!
/:a/index.html              /:a/             301!
/:a/:b/index.html           /:a/:b/          301!
/:a/:b/:c/index.html        /:a/:b/:c/       301!
/:a/:b/:c/:d/index.html     /:a/:b/:c/:d/    301!

# Tag and tech pages used to be addressed by their raw label, so the same page
# answered to "/blog/tags/SEO & Content/", to the percent-encoded version of it,
# and to nothing else. Search Console counted those as duplicates of each other.
# The pages now live at a lowercase hyphenated slug; these keep the addresses
# Google already crawled pointing at the new one instead of at a 404.
#
# No force flag here on purpose. These only fire when nothing is served at the
# old address, which after the rename is exactly the case. A forced rule would
# also match the new lowercase path if Netlify ever compares paths without
# regard to case, and that is a redirect loop.
/blog/tags/AI%20&%20Web%20Design    /blog/tags/ai-web-design/    301
/blog/tags/AI%20&%20Web%20Design/*    /blog/tags/ai-web-design/    301
